#
# Worked example: Principle 9, contestable / vantage-indexed compliance. Two
# assessors — a senior human reviewer and an automated linter — judge the SAME
# gmeow:Event against the SAME recommendation gmeow:Norm and DISAGREE: one
# holds the norm was complied with, the other holds it was not. Both
# gmeow:ComplianceAssessment claims coexist in the graph, each scoped to its
# own gmeow:vantage; there is no global, assessor-free verdict, and the
# disagreement is not an inconsistency to resolve — it is data (P9), the same
# move `graph/norm-claims` makes at scale for the shipped `advice.tier.active`
# demonstrator claim.
@prefix gmeow: <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/> .
@prefix ex:    <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/examples/norms/> .
@prefix rdfs:  <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#> .
@prefix xsd:   <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#> .

ex:styleAuthority a gmeow:Organization ; gmeow:name "Editorial Style Board"@x-gmeow-english .

# --- A RECOMMENDATION norm (the soft-tier mirror of an obligation): the norm
#     names its gmeow:normIssuer — there is no ought, only ought-according-to.
ex:activeVoiceNorm a gmeow:Norm ;
    rdfs:label            "Prefer active-voice phrasing in commit messages"@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:deonticModality gmeow:deonticRecommendation ;
    gmeow:normIssuer      ex:styleAuthority .

# --- The single event both assessors are judging.
ex:eventTypeCodeReview a gmeow:EventType ; rdfs:label "code review"@x-gmeow-english .

ex:commitReview a gmeow:Event ;
    rdfs:label                "Commit message review"@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:eventType            ex:eventTypeCodeReview ;
    gmeow:eventTime            "2026-06-20T09:30:00Z"^^xsd:dateTime ;
    gmeow:eventTemporalFrame   gmeow:temporalFrameUTCGregorian .

# --- Two standpoints: the assessors' vantages, both sharpening the universal
#     standpoint (neither is privileged over the other).
ex:seniorReviewerView a gmeow:Standpoint ; gmeow:sharpens gmeow:universalStandpoint .
ex:automatedLinterView a gmeow:Standpoint ; gmeow:sharpens gmeow:universalStandpoint .

# --- Ruling 1: the senior human reviewer holds the norm was complied with.
ex:seniorReviewerRuling a gmeow:ComplianceAssessment ;
    gmeow:assessedEvent     ex:commitReview ;
    gmeow:assessedNorm      ex:activeVoiceNorm ;
    gmeow:complianceVerdict gmeow:verdictHeld ;
    gmeow:vantage           ex:seniorReviewerView .

# --- Ruling 2: the automated linter holds the SAME norm, over the SAME event,
#     was NOT complied with. Both rulings coexist — no global verdict (P9).
ex:automatedLinterRuling a gmeow:ComplianceAssessment ;
    gmeow:assessedEvent     ex:commitReview ;
    gmeow:assessedNorm      ex:activeVoiceNorm ;
    gmeow:complianceVerdict gmeow:verdictNotHeld ;
    gmeow:vantage           ex:automatedLinterView .
